---- what has itself in it
    dict == dict => RecursionError
    dict != dict => RecursionError
    list == list => RecursionError
    list < list => RecursionError
    list >= list => RecursionError
    a tuple in a list => RecursionError
    a list in a dict => RecursionError
    deque == deque => RecursionError
    in => RecursionError
    index() => RecursionError
    count() => RecursionError
    remove() => RecursionError
    sorted() => RecursionError
    max() => RecursionError
    the very same is equal => (True, True, 0, 1)
    repr() => ('[[...]]', "{'a': {...}}")
    dict values => RecursionError
    dict items => RecursionError
---- what is very deep
    list == ends
    tuple == ends
    dict == ends
    slice == ends
    list < ends
    sorted() ends
    repr() of a list ends
    of a tuple ends
    of a dict ends
    hash() of a frozenset ends
    of a slice ends
    filter() ends
    enumerate() ends
    islice() ends
    isinstance() of a tuple ends
    issubclass() of a tuple ends
    SimpleNamespace == ends
    staticmethod ends
    a generator ends
---- and afterwards all is as it was
True True True True [1] True
---- the hash of a frozenset is worked out once
60 60 True True True
True 0 True True
True True None False True
